#: ../../source/guides/formats/tutorials/diagnosing-a-format.md:1
msgid "Diagnosing a format that already runs"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/tutorials/diagnosing-a-format.md:3
msgid ""
"The harder job is not the empty page. It is the format that runs, "
"produces thousands of plausible rows, and is quietly wrong about some of "
"them. This page is a method for that, written from a real investigation."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/tutorials/diagnosing-a-format.md:7
msgid "Start from the log, not from the PDF"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/tutorials/diagnosing-a-format.md:9
msgid ""
"Every run writes `.log.csv` next to its output. It is a table, not a wall"
" of text, and it exists so that the first question — *where should I even"
" look?* — can be answered by counting."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/tutorials/diagnosing-a-format.md:25
msgid ""
"Then count by *kind* of event rather than by document, because that is "
"what tells you whether you are looking at one problem or twenty. In the "
"run above, 188 rows turned out to be four distinct phenomena, of which "
"two were not problems at all."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/tutorials/diagnosing-a-format.md:29
msgid ""
"Each row carries the report, the page, the full activity path, and "
"coordinates — the row and column of the cell it is about. That is "
"deliberate: the point of an event is that you can go back to the report "
"and *find the thing*."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/tutorials/diagnosing-a-format.md:33
msgid "What the events mean"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/tutorials/diagnosing-a-format.md
msgid "The message says"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/tutorials/diagnosing-a-format.md
msgid "It means"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/tutorials/diagnosing-a-format.md
msgid "Usually"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/tutorials/diagnosing-a-format.md
msgid "`… sits on the edge of the admissible range - kept`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/tutorials/diagnosing-a-format.md
msgid ""
"a value landed exactly on a boundary of its domain — a holding worth "
"zero, a position that is the whole fund"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/tutorials/diagnosing-a-format.md
msgid "fine, and kept on purpose"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/tutorials/diagnosing-a-format.md
msgid "`forced \"…\" to \"…\" to read it as a number`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/tutorials/diagnosing-a-format.md
msgid ""
"the cell was not a clean number and noise had to be stripped before it "
"could be read"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/tutorials/diagnosing-a-format.md
msgid "worth a look"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/tutorials/diagnosing-a-format.md
msgid "`… - holding skipped` / `page skipped`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/tutorials/diagnosing-a-format.md
msgid ""
"something did not satisfy the output schema and was dropped, with the "
"field named"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/tutorials/diagnosing-a-format.md
msgid "a real loss, always read it"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/tutorials/diagnosing-a-format.md
msgid "`the … is missing: N cells past the anchor`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/tutorials/diagnosing-a-format.md
msgid "the grid was walked and the expected cell was not there"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/tutorials/diagnosing-a-format.md
msgid "a column mapping to re-check"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/tutorials/diagnosing-a-format.md:42
msgid "Two habits follow from that table."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/tutorials/diagnosing-a-format.md:44
#, python-format
msgid ""
"**A warning is not automatically a bug.** The engine warns about zero-"
"valued holdings because zero is on the edge of what is admissible, not "
"because zero is wrong — a security written off is worth exactly nothing, "
"and discarding it would throw away the very fact worth reporting. In the "
"run above, 116 of the 188 rows were holdings rounding to 0.00% of net "
"assets. All correct."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/tutorials/diagnosing-a-format.md:49
msgid ""
"**And silence is not automatically correctness.** The events you get are "
"the ones the engine knew how to doubt. Nothing warns you that a column "
"mapping is off by one and every market value belongs to the row above."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/tutorials/diagnosing-a-format.md:53
msgid "Two examples of the same message meaning opposite things"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/tutorials/diagnosing-a-format.md:55
msgid ""
"Both of these produced `forced \"-X\" to \"X\" to read it as a number`. "
"One was noise, the other was a real defect. Telling them apart is the "
"whole skill."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/tutorials/diagnosing-a-format.md:58
msgid "The false positive"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/tutorials/diagnosing-a-format.md:60
msgid ""
"A fund's Statement of Net Assets is laid out so that assets plus "
"liabilities equal net assets, so `Total Liabilities` is printed with a "
"minus:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/tutorials/diagnosing-a-format.md:69
msgid ""
"The output schema wants a magnitude — it checks that `liabilities + "
"net_assets == tot_assets` — so the extracted value was right all along. "
"The warning was an artefact of a convention, and the fix was to make the "
"convention explicit in the format rather than to leave the engine "
"guessing."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/tutorials/diagnosing-a-format.md:73
msgid ""
"The check that settled it took one command: compare the same field across"
" every format that does *not* warn, and see what value they carry. They "
"were all positive magnitudes."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/tutorials/diagnosing-a-format.md:76
msgid "The real defect"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/tutorials/diagnosing-a-format.md:78
msgid "The same message, on a different report, was hiding this in the output:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/tutorials/diagnosing-a-format.md:84
msgid ""
"A **written put option** — a short position — recorded as a long holding "
"of 30,900 USD in Exxon Mobil, and classified as a bond. The minus sign "
"that said \"short\" had been stripped."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/tutorials/diagnosing-a-format.md:87
msgid ""
"Nothing about the message distinguished the two cases. What distinguished"
" them was asking, in each case, **what the sign meant in that field**: a "
"presentation convention on a magnitude, or the difference between owning "
"something and owing it."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/tutorials/diagnosing-a-format.md:91
msgid "Reproducing it on one page"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/tutorials/diagnosing-a-format.md:93
msgid ""
"Once you have a suspect page, the modes of `inspect-page` are a decision "
"procedure rather than a menu."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/tutorials/diagnosing-a-format.md
msgid "Your question"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/tutorials/diagnosing-a-format.md
msgid "Mode"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/tutorials/diagnosing-a-format.md
msgid "how is this text actually typeset?"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/tutorials/diagnosing-a-format.md
msgid "`structured` with `--strings`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/tutorials/diagnosing-a-format.md
msgid "did the engine read the columns the way I read them?"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/tutorials/diagnosing-a-format.md
msgid "`table_ascii` or `table_md`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/tutorials/diagnosing-a-format.md
msgid "what was found on the page?"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/tutorials/diagnosing-a-format.md
msgid "`pdf_blks`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/tutorials/diagnosing-a-format.md
msgid "what survived filtering?"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/tutorials/diagnosing-a-format.md
msgid "`txt_blks`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/tutorials/diagnosing-a-format.md
msgid "what was it turned into?"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/tutorials/diagnosing-a-format.md
msgid "`results`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/tutorials/diagnosing-a-format.md:104
msgid ""
"The table modes are the ones people forget, and they are the fastest "
"route to a class of bug that is otherwise invisible. Here is the page "
"that held the Exxon put, rendered as a table:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/tutorials/diagnosing-a-format.md:115
msgid ""
"Eight columns, because **the page holds two tables side by side**. That "
"single observation explains a whole family of confusing results, and it "
"is worth internalising:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/tutorials/diagnosing-a-format.md:118
msgid ""
"reading order is **column-major** — down the left table, then down the "
"right one;"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/tutorials/diagnosing-a-format.md:119
msgid ""
"a section of the report can therefore open partway down one column and "
"continue in the *other* column, or on the *next page*;"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/tutorials/diagnosing-a-format.md:121
msgid ""
"so a rule of the form *\"everything below y on this page\"* is wrong "
"twice over."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/tutorials/diagnosing-a-format.md:123
msgid ""
"In the report above, the heading that opens the short-positions section "
"sits in the right-hand column of page 316, and the section runs on "
"through the left-hand column of page 317. That is how a put option ended "
"up two pages away from the heading that explained it."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/tutorials/diagnosing-a-format.md:127
msgid "Choosing the layer: is this the format's problem or the engine's?"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/tutorials/diagnosing-a-format.md:129
msgid ""
"The same symptom lives in different places, and putting the fix in the "
"wrong one is how a repository accumulates workarounds."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/tutorials/diagnosing-a-format.md
msgid "Ask"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/tutorials/diagnosing-a-format.md
msgid "If yes, it belongs to"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/tutorials/diagnosing-a-format.md
msgid "would another report with this layout need the same handling?"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/tutorials/diagnosing-a-format.md
msgid "**the format**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/tutorials/diagnosing-a-format.md
msgid "does the report state something the engine has no way to know?"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/tutorials/diagnosing-a-format.md
msgid "would every format be wrong in the same way on this input?"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/tutorials/diagnosing-a-format.md
msgid "**the engine**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/tutorials/diagnosing-a-format.md
msgid "is the engine producing a value the report does not contain?"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/tutorials/diagnosing-a-format.md:139
msgid ""
"The Exxon case answers the last one: the report said `-200`, the output "
"said `200`. No format configuration should have to compensate for that, "
"so the fix went into the engine — and it went in as *stop coercing*, not "
"as *stop warning*."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/tutorials/diagnosing-a-format.md:144
msgid ""
"Never silence a diagnostic at the point where it is the only thing "
"standing between a wrong value and the output. If a coercion is what "
"makes an invalid value pass validation, the fix is to remove the coercion"
" and let the field or the row be rejected with a message naming it — not "
"to quieten the message. A quiet log and a wrong number is the worst of "
"the four combinations."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/tutorials/diagnosing-a-format.md:150
msgid "Proving that a fix loses nothing"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/tutorials/diagnosing-a-format.md:152
msgid ""
"This is the part that is easy to skip and expensive to skip. A change "
"that removes bad rows can remove good ones, and *\"I checked and it looks"
" right\"* does not scale to a thousand pages. Three measurements, in "
"increasing strength:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/tutorials/diagnosing-a-format.md:156
msgid "**1. The suite you already have.**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/tutorials/diagnosing-a-format.md:163
msgid ""
"Every format's whole-document output is pinned, so anything you disturbed"
" anywhere shows up. Do this before you believe anything else."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/tutorials/diagnosing-a-format.md:166
msgid ""
"**2. A real run, diffed.** The suite searches a small built-in company "
"list, so a change that only affects companies outside it passes "
"invisibly. Run the engine against the input database you actually care "
"about, before and after, and diff the outputs."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/tutorials/diagnosing-a-format.md:170
msgid ""
"**3. A run that emits everything.** Even a real database only surfaces "
"rows that matched a company. To see *every* row your change touches, "
"build a throwaway input database with a single company whose regex "
"matches anything:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/tutorials/diagnosing-a-format.md:179
msgid ""
"Every row of the report is now emitted, and the diff covers rows a "
"realistic database would never have reached. Expect noise — bare numbers "
"get \"matched\" as company names — but this is the measurement that turns"
" *\"nothing else seems to have changed\"* into a count."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/tutorials/diagnosing-a-format.md:183
msgid ""
"In the investigation this page is drawn from, those three steps produced:"
" 259 tests passing, exactly four rows removed from the real run and "
"nothing altered, and, under the catch-all, confirmation that every "
"removed row was one the engine had previously emitted with a falsified "
"sign."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/tutorials/diagnosing-a-format.md:187
msgid "When the reference outputs must change"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/tutorials/diagnosing-a-format.md:189
msgid ""
"Sometimes a genuine improvement makes tests fail, because `out/**` is the"
" repository's specification and the specification was written against the"
" old behaviour."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/tutorials/diagnosing-a-format.md:192
msgid ""
"Regenerating is a deliberate act, and the rule is simple: **classify "
"every single difference before you touch anything.** Not \"29 tests fail,"
" let me regenerate\" — but a list, of the shape:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/tutorials/diagnosing-a-format.md:195
msgid "13 coupon values, all corrected: `10.25%` was being read as `0.25%`;"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/tutorials/diagnosing-a-format.md:196
msgid "14 per-page fixtures carrying those same coupons;"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/tutorials/diagnosing-a-format.md:197
msgid ""
"2 cells where `Intesa Sanpaolo SpA 7% / perpetual` moved from equity to "
"**bond** — a perpetual has no maturity date, so it was only recognised "
"once the coupon could be read;"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/tutorials/diagnosing-a-format.md:199
msgid "no rows lost, no row counts moved anywhere."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/tutorials/diagnosing-a-format.md:201
msgid ""
"Once every difference has a reason, regenerate, and write the reasons "
"down. If you cannot explain a difference, you have found a second bug "
"rather than finished with the first."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/tutorials/diagnosing-a-format.md:204
msgid "The shape of the whole thing"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/tutorials/diagnosing-a-format.md:215
msgid ""
"The payoff, in the run this page follows: 188 log rows became 175, the "
"twenty-one misleading warnings became four accurate errors that name the "
"security and the field, and coupon correctness went from 2695 of 2758 to "
"2817 of 2817."
msgstr ""

